{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Under all the heavens he directs it</b> — And \"his light\" is the lightning. And Rav Saadia the Gaon [Saadia] said: that it speaks of the Place [i.e., God]. And this is not correct, for it does not connect to the verses above and below, and the word ישרהו (\"he directs it\") is like משרת ענבים, and this expression is well-known in the words of our Rabbis of blessed memory: שורין. And some say: that it is from the root ישר, but this is far-fetched."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:48.287510088Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}